  "future_pr_comment_draft": "I ran the Linux gate on candidate head `5df2caa0e59a9bbbd0d6e91e74bfbfc80797b69f` (parent `219fee78bf7cae5039e50fe885108a1d4937ccd3`). The focused `PrimitiveFieldTypeTest` and `TestICUCollationField` suites each passed 9/9 with no skips. The neighboring core and ICU DocValues suites also passed, including `TestSortableTextField.testWhiteboxCreateFields`, `TestUseDocValuesAsStored.testBinary`, and the DocValues test classes.\n\nFor an actual multivalued case, `DocValuesMultiTest.testBoolDocValuesMatch` indexes a document with both `true` and `false` values for the same field and passed. The new core and ICU collation DocValues-only tests exercise both single- and multivalued configurations; the ignored-field helper also covers both shapes, and its Trie test loops over all five legacy Trie field classes. `./gradlew check -x test` succeeded as well.\n\nThere was one unrelated assumption skip in `TestTrie.testTrieFacet_PrecisionStep`: its randomized configuration was points=true and DocValues=false, while that facet test requires DocValues. The required ignored-Trie coverage ran and passed. These results cover the exercised preservation cases; they are not a mutation proof or an exhaustive test of every DocValues path. The public PR is still at `00292cd3729126194235e939afe38e351d850c70`; this gate verifies the separate candidate head above, and no PR update or comment has been made.",
